{"id": "EUVD-2026-80430", "enisaUuid": "667318d3-f571-399b-b851-43f84a73a284", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: fix valid block count leak on data block allocation failure\n\nIn __allocate_data_block(), when allocating a new data block\n(dn->data_blkaddr == NULL_ADDR), inc_valid_block_count() is\ncalled first to increment total_valid_block_count and i_blocks.\nIf the subsequent f2fs_allocate_data_block() fails, the function\nreturns the error directly without rolling back the\nalready-incremented block counts, causing a permanent leak.\n\nFix this by calling dec_valid_block_count() to undo the\nincrement before returning the error. The condition\nold_blkaddr == NULL_ADDR precisely identifies the case where\ninc_valid_block_count() was called.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d50b6d47e5671ff6a25834c5906d443356191f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dde99df5a9d3b0ca6ac0a86f98799685f7399432", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/931e1aa4d44c52ff8e0feb38420a8827c62e886b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f9af07ecc1ab486038373db6ae0436c5d674b19"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c5cf-c6gm-hv9c", "CVE-2026-89830"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06ed7677-1b82-3cf5-a42f-98aed022f1b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "14037666-bf58-3206-8b97-24c8afc070e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "1fb8e22d-8020-351a-9673-8be9177072a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d009e048d7cfcc21d400f2aba4c8bacbdebbd47 <2d50b6d47e5671ff6a25834c5906d443356191f0"}, {"id": "26e3bafa-c1dc-3c5f-9ac2-c6380bd7e547", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "51689397-9ca4-30b2-89e3-bb279e460aa2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d009e048d7cfcc21d400f2aba4c8bacbdebbd47 <0f9af07ecc1ab486038373db6ae0436c5d674b19"}, {"id": "869f311b-d9d0-375c-b034-0a199ee7469a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "a7bae9ee-7e43-3f44-9e35-7ed1e19de485", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "b48f3a19-cc4a-347a-8f08-8652b983c312", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d009e048d7cfcc21d400f2aba4c8bacbdebbd47 <931e1aa4d44c52ff8e0feb38420a8827c62e886b"}, {"id": "d6b71910-d6b5-35a6-9a9d-339dbaa39ec2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f70fab27-46af-312b-a079-3bed33228000", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d009e048d7cfcc21d400f2aba4c8bacbdebbd47 <dde99df5a9d3b0ca6ac0a86f98799685f7399432"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "260dc539-748d-3748-8f64-634cf8687984", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}